## Practical information

Peloid procedures are available at most Ensana spa hotels in Marienbad. A single procedure lasts 20–40 minutes depending on the form, plus the rest period. Individual peat baths can also be booked without a comprehensive spa stay; within a treatment programme they are usually included in the package. In the treatment plan, peat is usually combined with the [drinking cure](/en/mineral-springs), CO₂ baths and exercise therapy.

## Frequently asked questions about peloid therapy

### What is Marienbad healing peat?

A natural peloid from the bogs of the Slavkov Forest, made up of partly decomposed plant remains and containing humic acids, fulvic acids and mineral salts. The spa has extracted and processed it, and used it for wraps, baths and packs, since the 19th century.

### What is the difference between a peat wrap and a peat bath?

For a wrap, warm peat at 38–42 °C is applied to individual parts of the body and washed off after 20–30 minutes. A peat bath is a full-body bath in a mixture of peat and mineral water at the same temperature; it lasts 20–30 minutes and is followed by at least half an hour of rest.

### Why does peat warm differently from a hot bath?

Peat has low thermal conductivity, so it releases its stored heat slowly and evenly. That is why a bath at around 40 °C is pleasant, whereas a water bath of the same temperature would be uncomfortable for most people.

### Which conditions is peloid therapy used for?

Above all for diseases of the musculoskeletal system in indication group VII — osteoarthritis, chronic back pain, painful tendon and muscle insertions, rheumatic diseases in a quiescent phase and conditions after injuries and orthopaedic surgery — and for skin diseases in group X, namely atopic eczema and psoriasis.

### Is peloid therapy suitable for everyone?

No. The spa physician decides on inclusion at the initial examination. Heat procedures are not given, for example, in acute inflammation, fever, circulatory failure, shortly after deep vein thrombosis, with open wounds and in pregnancy.

### Where is peloid therapy offered?

Peat wraps, baths and packs under medical supervision are offered in Marienbad by the Ensana Centrální Lázně hotel; peloid procedures are also available at the other Ensana spa hotels.
